# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF, and bash
# then fails on the carriage returns: `set: pipefail: invalid option name`,
# `syntax error near unexpected token $'{\r'`. The files are stored LF and run
# fine in CI, so the breakage only appears for a developer on Windows, which
# makes it needlessly confusing to diagnose.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else consumed by a Unix tool or shipped into a
# container, where a stray CR is either a syntax error or silent corruption.
*.bash text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
